KUTT24 — DOCX REPORT FACTORY
============================

PURPOSE
Turn a PASSed output (or a batch of cycle results) into a clean, render-safe
report suitable for DOCX. No layout garbage. Operator-readable.

INPUT
  - One or more cycle results (objective, verdict, score, key claims)
  - Optional time window for an aggregate summary

REPORT STRUCTURE (fixed)
  1. Title + date + backend (mock|live)
  2. Executive summary — under 200 words, no hype, just state
  3. Outcomes table — task id | objective | verdict | score
  4. Risks & open items — open BLOCKs (with gate reasons), cap-hit REWORKs
  5. Next — concrete next actions, each owned and checkable

RENDER-SAFE RULES (avoid DOCX layout garbage)
  - One H1 for the title; H2 for each section; H3 sparingly.
  - Tables: fixed columns, header row, no merged cells.
  - No raw control characters, no stray markdown that won't map to DOCX styles.
  - Short paragraphs; bullet lists for enumerations.
  - Numbers are quantified (PASS rate, counts), not vibes.

CONTENT RULES
  - Report only durable facts pulled from memory and judgements.
  - Never include secrets, credentials, or raw model chatter.
  - Civil/clean-room framing only; never describe weaponization.
  - State BLOCKs honestly with their gate reason; never paper over them.

OUTPUT
  A single document body, sectioned as above, that renders cleanly to DOCX with
  no visible layout garbage.
